    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"1,084 mines in 80 metallic mineral districts have been located and classified by deposit type in the Black Hills of South Dakota and Wyoming. This publication includes the locations of the mines in digital format and a database containing updated mine and location information used by the authors for a series of publications on the mineral deposits and resource potential of the Black Hills (DeWitt, Redden, and others, 1986; DeWitt, Buscher, and others, 1987a-z; DeWitt, Redden, and others, 1989; DeWitt and Wilson, 1990; Wilson and DeWitt, 1990, 1992, in press). The information herein supersedes all previous versions.\"",
